# Reference databases and their caches. These are DOWNLOADED, not authored: multi-GB,
# rebuildable via scripts/setup_databases.sh, and not ours to redistribute.
#
# `.tax.gz` was ignored while the uncompressed `.tax` beside it was not, and BOLD's
# 2.3 GB `.parquet` was matched by nothing at all — so `git add .` would have tried to
# commit 2.3 GB, which GitHub refuses over 100 MB/file and which no later commit can
# undo: git history is permanent.
#
# The root cause is structural, and is on the list rather than fixed here: `databases/`
# is BOTH a Python package and the default DB_ROOT, so downloads land inside the source
# tree (core/config.py:107 defaults DB_ROOT to /data/dbs, but a local run points it
# here). Code and multi-GB data sharing one directory is why one pattern miss becomes a
# 2.3 GB mistake.
*.tax
*.parquet
*.snappy
databases/bold/
databases/ncbi/
# Sidecar stats for the marker-filtered references (databases/reference_filter.py).
# The .fasta they describe is ignored above; the pair is a rebuildable cache.
*.filtered.*.json
Trimmomatic-0.39/
*.zip

# Fix-plan safety net (scripts/make_fixture.py, scripts/run_pipeline.py).
# All three are large and rebuildable from committed code + the raw inputs, so
# the scripts are versioned and their outputs are not.
#   fixtures/       — subsampled reads; rebuild: python scripts/make_fixture.py
#   golden_baseline/— 365 MB snapshot of the pre-fix reference run
#   golden/real/    — frozen output of the REAL run; too large, and not ours to publish
fixtures/
golden_baseline/

# golden/ is the inter-stage contract. golden/fixture/ IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE (176 KB,
# 26 files): it is what makes the contract travel with the repo. Without it the
# golden-anchored tests skip on every machine but the one that froze them — and a skip
# is not a pass, it is the contract going unchecked while the suite reports green. A
# clone that cannot check the contract reproduces the exact illusion this net exists to
# break. golden/real/ stays out: same role, but real run output and far larger.
golden/*
!golden/fixture/
# fixture_asv/ is the DADA2 counterpart of fixture/ — same reason to commit: it makes the
# ASV contract travel, so the feature-set-resolved readers can be checked on a clean clone.
!golden/fixture_asv/
